</div>
<p class="meta-info">Expect historical note: task brief listed 11 large, 2 medium, 35 small, 32 tiny, 29 unknown for same 109 total — current live counts above reflect latest <code>servers.js</code> as of {{ site.reviewed }}. Use filters on <a href="/">tracker</a> and <a href="/servers/">servers</a> to browse each tier.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
<h2>By-era grouping — via vocab.js ERA</h2>
<p class="meta-info" style="margin-top:0"><code>ERA</code> collapses <code>tag</code> into navigation eras. Ordering follows <code>ERA_ORDER</code>. Vanilla includes Vanilla, Vanilla+, Classless.</p>
{% set groups = servers | groupByEra %}
<div style="overflow-x:auto">
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14.5px">
<thead><tr style="text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><th style="padding:8px 10px">Era</th><th style="padding:8px 10px">Count</th><th style="padding:8px 10px">Share</th><th style="padding:8px 10px">Browse</th><th style="padding:8px 10px">Visual</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for g in groups %}
<tr style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)"><td style="padding:8px 10px"><strong>{{ g.era }}</strong></td><td style="padding:8px 10px">{{ g.servers.length }}</td><td style="padding:8px 10px">{{ ((g.servers.length/total)*100) | round(1) }}%</td><td style="padding:8px 10px"><a href="/{{ g.era | lower | slugify }}/">{{ g.era | lower }}</a></td><td style="padding:8px 10px"><div style="background:var(--panel-2);border:1px solid var(--border);height:10px;border-radius:999px;overflow:hidden;max-width:220px"><div style="width:{{ ((g.servers.length/total)*100) | round(1) }}%;height:100%;background:var(--gold)"></div></div></td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="meta-info">Totals reflect <code>groupByEra(servers)</code> directly, so renaming a tag in <code>servers.js</code> automatically moves it here. See expansion pages below for full lists and guides.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel">
<h2>Category guides — how to read tiers</h2>
<div class="cp-cols" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr">
<div>
<h3>Large ({{ cLarge }})</h3>
<p>Persistent high concurrency, frequent queues, stable auction house. Best for instant groups. Expect competition. Example filter: <a href="/">tracker</a> → Pop Large.</p>
<h3>Medium ({{ cMedium }})</h3>
<p>Healthy population without megaserver pressure. Raids fill, world feels alive, names still recognizable.</p>
<h3>Small ({{ cSmall }})</h3>
<p>Niche and often blizzlike. 50–300 concurrent, Discord-driven scheduling. Choose for authentic rates and tight guilds.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3>Tiny ({{ cTiny }})</h3>
<p>Early, experimental, or solo-dev realms. 0–50 online. Good for testing or seeding a community, not for immediate endgame.</p>
<h3>Unknown ({{ cUnknown }})</h3>
<p>No verifiable number — in-development, archived dead, or silent projects. Always check <code>updated</code> and <code>release</code> on the server card before planning.</p>
<h3>Using both tables</h3>
<p>Cross-reference tier with era. A small Vanilla realm behaves differently from a small WotLK realm due to core maturity. Start with era, then tier.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

